  **     At the same time, you are using a relatively low-quality integration grid
  **     (302 points or less per grid shell around each atom), indicating that these are
  **     light settings or similar.
  **     For cases in which the total energy is the only objective, your force criterion is typically
  **     too tight. As noted in the manual, 'relax_geometry bfgs 5e-3' is usually more than
  **     sufficient.
  **     In your run, the maximum force encountered on any single atom was already lower than
  **     max_force =   0.00010932 eV/AA in geometry step number      116.
  **     If your total energy did not decrease significantly from that point onwards,
  **     then that relaxed geometry and total energy may already have been good enough.
  **     You should finalize the relaxation with 'intermediate' or 'tight' settings.
  **
  ** (1) Use denser integration grids to see if this is just related to grid quality.
